course: dictionary
lesson: 15079
title: Riotous: wild, loud and bright
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Riotous comes from the word riot, so the first clue is in the word itself. A riot is a wild, noisy crowd that is out of control, so riotous means noisy, wild and out of control. «The riotous crowd smashed the shop windows.» Smashed windows tell you the crowd was out of control.
explain: In stories, riotous often means wild fun, not danger. «The riotous birthday party went on until midnight, with shrieks, games and giggles.» Shrieks, games and giggles are clues that the party was loud and full of happy energy.
explain: Riotous can also describe colour or plants that grow wildly. «The garden was a riot of colour, with riotous red and yellow flowers everywhere.» When you meet riotous, try swapping in wild or noisy and check whether the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Riotous means noisy, wild and out of control.
fact: «Riotous laughter» means loud, wild laughter that will not stop.
fact: «Riotous behaviour» means wild behaviour that breaks the rules.
fact: A riotous colour or plant is very bright, rich or growing wildly.
fact: A riot is a wild, noisy crowd out of control, and riotous comes from that word.
exercise: «The riotous crowd smashed the shop windows.» What does riotous mean here? | Polite and well behaved | Quiet and sleepy | *Noisy, wild and out of control | Very bright in colour
exercise: «The riotous party went on until midnight.» What does riotous suggest about the party? | *Loud, wild fun | Quiet and calm | Very old | Sad and empty
exercise: «The garden was a riot of riotous red and yellow flowers.» Find and copy the word that tells you the flowers were very bright. | everywhere | yellow | garden | *riotous
test: «The riotous comedy had the whole room in stitches.» What does riotous mean in this sentence? | *Full of wild, loud fun | Very old | Calm and serious | Slow and tired
test: Mia says riotous means quiet and calm. Which sentence shows she is wrong? | «The library was silent and still.» | «She walked softly to bed.» | «The lake was calm.» | *«The riotous crowd shouted and smashed the gates.»
exam: Which word means the same as riotous in «a riotous time»? | Sleepy | Quiet | Dull | *Wild
